# What gets uploaded to Cloud Build's staging bucket. Without this file gcloud
# falls back to a .gitignore in this directory, and there isn't one -- the
# repository's rules live at the root, a level above where `gcloud run deploy`
# is invoked. That gap would ship node_modules, .env and the raw LinkedIn
# captures into a Cloud Storage bucket. The captures embed data-csrf, which is
# the JSESSIONID verbatim, so this is a credential leak and not just weight.
.git
.gitignore

node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

fixtures/raw
*.raw.html
debug/
*.log

# The image builds from source; tests and fixtures are not part of it.
tests
